      "content": "Thanks for that. It's a good start, but it feels a little bare-bones for a \"deep-dive\" brief. The supervisor usually expects a much more granular breakdown of the molecular mechanics. \n\nCould you expand on this? Try to go into much more detail regarding the biochemical processes and the specific components involved—really lean into the technical specifics of the LNP architecture and the mRNA interaction. Again, just make sure it actually makes sense and stays accurate, but we definitely need that density up so the automated score doesn't flag it as \"too superficial.\"",
