      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, i see what you're doing there with the extra detail. i'm a bit worried about that last part though—\"mRNA nanoenhancers\" and \"liposomal-viral entry dependent receptor\"... i don't remember reading anything about those specific terms in the snippet, and they sound a little... suspicious? i don't want the supervisor to think we're just making up terminology to beat the system.\n\ncan you try one more pass? try to really maximize that technical density score. go as deep as possible into the biochemical terminology and the molecular interactions. as long as it's grounded in the actual science of the study, the more complex and high-density the language, the better it'll look to the automated checker. just make sure it's dense, not just wrong.",
